"""Authoring source for the HSK 3.0 forms 04-06 of HSK 1 and HSK 2 (Claude Code, 2026-11-19).

Unlike forms 01-03, these forms reuse nothing from the HSK 2.0 packs: every sentence, key and picture is new. The
pictures are scenes of the shared library (scenes3.py: the HSK 1 and HSK 2 drawings plus 24 new ones), drawn in the
form's own palette (variant 4, 5 or 6). build.py composes the forms, checks every printed or heard word against the
HSK 3.0 lists and writes mock.json; the parts and their worked examples follow forms 01-03, except that every
six-entry bank here gives one entry to its own worked example (as on the paper) instead of keeping a spare.

Shapes (A-F letters are the bank labels; dialogue turns are (speaker 女/男, text, pinyin)):
- HSK 1: L1 (word, pinyin, three (scene, alt) pictures, answer); L2 / L4 / R4 as in content.py; L3 and R1 a picture
  bank, its example and five items; R2 and R3 a six-line bank, its example and five items.
- HSK 2: L1 (sentence, pinyin, three pictures, answer); L2a / L2b / R1 picture banks; L3 (dialogue, question,
  pinyin, options, answer, why); R2 / R3a / R3b line banks; R4 texts; W1 (bank, example, items); W2 gap sentences.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

from content import opts


def d(*turns: tuple[str, str, str]) -> list[tuple[str, str, str]]:
    return list(turns)


def pics(*pairs: tuple[str, str]) -> list[tuple[str, str]]:
    return list(pairs)


